# GPU-fit tuning: Qwen3.8-27B BF16 on Strix Halo (MACHINE=strixhalo).
#
# Sourced by the launchers AFTER models/qwen3.8-27b.env and BEFORE
# profiles/strixhalo/default.env.
#
# This is the fleet's flagship placement for the 27B: 108 GiB of unified GTT is
# the only pool here that holds BF16 weights AND the full native context with
# room to spare, so run it unquantized. Dense model, so there is no MoE to
# offload -- do NOT add --n-cpu-moe; every layer belongs on the GPU.
#
# KV math (verified from GGUF metadata 2026-08-14): 16 of 65 blocks are full
# attention (full_attention_interval 4), 4 KV heads x head_dim 256 x (K+V)
# = 32,768 elements/token -> ~34 KiB/token at q8_0. The 48 Gated DeltaNet
# blocks hold a constant-size SSM state (conv_kernel 4, state_size 128,
# inner_size 6144), NOT a per-token KV cache, which is why a 27B here is
# cheaper per token of context than a dense 27B would be.
#
# Memory budget vs ~108 GiB GTT:
#   weights (BF16, 2 shards)         50.9 GiB
#   KV @ 262,144 tok, q8_0 K+V        8.5 GiB
#   vision projector (mmproj BF16)    0.9 GiB
#   compute buffers @ ubatch 1024    ~2   GiB
#   DeltaNet SSM state               ~0.1 GiB   (ctx-independent)
#   ------------------------------------------
#   total                            ~62 GiB / 108 GiB GTT   (~46 GiB spare)
#
# Native max context, so no rope scaling: 262144 is the model's trained length
# and needs no YaRN. For more than that use qwen3.8-27b-1m (YaRN-gated) rather
# than raising CTX_SIZE here -- past 262144 unscaled the model degrades.
#
# Concurrency note: --parallel SPLITS this context across slots, it does not
# multiply it. Each slot gets CTX_SIZE/PARALLEL, while VRAM scales with total KV
# tokens. Keep PARALLEL at the launcher default of 1 to give a single request
# the whole 262K window. There is headroom here to raise both if you want
# concurrency -- e.g. PARALLEL=2 with CTX_SIZE unchanged costs another 8.5 GiB
# and still fits.
: "${CTX_SIZE:=262144}"
: "${UBATCH:=1024}"
